## Context

Child of 0365, which settled the project's forge identity: one account, no
machine account, privilege separation by **token scope** rather than by account.

`AGENT_GH_TOKEN` is today a *classic* PAT with scopes `gist, read:org, repo,
workflow`. Classic scopes are account-wide: the token reaches every repository
the owner has, plus their gists. A fine-grained PAT restricted to
`MinhHaDuong/climate-finance-het` gives the agent exactly the access it uses and
bounds the blast radius of a leak — which is the scenario ticket 0343 exists to
bound.

This is the one step of 0365 an agent cannot perform: minting a PAT is a browser
action under the owner's account. Everything else 0365 decided has landed.

## Actions

1. Create a fine-grained PAT at github.com → Settings → Developer settings →
   Personal access tokens → Fine-grained tokens.
   - Resource owner: `MinhHaDuong`
   - Repository access: **Only select repositories** → `climate-finance-het`
   - Repository permissions:
     - Metadata: Read-only (mandatory, granted automatically)
     - Contents: Read and write — clone, push, branch
     - Pull requests: Read and write — open, review, merge
     - Issues: Read and write — the merge gate reads PR labels, which live on
       the issues endpoint
   - Nothing else. `workflow` is unnecessary (the repo has no
     `.github/workflows/`), and `gist` and `read:org` are unused.
   - Expiry: the author's call. Fine-grained PATs cannot be non-expiring; note
     the date, because every agent forge operation stops when it lapses.
2. Replace the value of `AGENT_GH_TOKEN` in `~/.config/keys/github.env`
   (mode 0600). No `KEYS=` change: one identity, one variable, so the rename
   form 0365 considered is not needed.

   **Superseded by what was done.** The author stored the new token under
   `AGENT_GH_TOKEN_CLIMATEFINANCE`, keeping the classic PAT addressable at
   `AGENT_GH_TOKEN`, and the `KEYS=` entry became the rename-on-export form
   `github:AGENT_GH_TOKEN_CLIMATEFINANCE=AGENT_GH_TOKEN`. That is the better
   arrangement and the plan above was wrong to rule it out: a fine-grained PAT
   is *per-repository* by construction, so the keystore will accumulate one
   github token per project and a bare `AGENT_GH_TOKEN` cannot name them all.
   The suffix names which repository the token is bounded to; the `KEYS=` line
   does the selection, exactly as the sibling
   `openrouter:OPENROUTER_API_KEY_CLIMATEFINANCE=OPENROUTER_API_KEY` entry
   already did. It also satisfies the invariant below for free — the classic
   PAT stays reachable under its own name during the swap instead of being
   overwritten.
3. Verify, in a shell that has *not* inherited the old value — `BASH_ENV`
   re-injects it, so use `env -i` or clear it first.

## Verification

All checks run under `env -i` so the old value could not be inherited, and by
behaviour rather than by inspecting any value.

- [x] `gh api user --jq .login` under the new token returns `MinhHaDuong`
- [x] `gh api repos/MinhHaDuong/climate-finance-het --jq .full_name` succeeds;
      PR, issue and label endpoints all read (3 open PRs, 20 labels)
- [x] Scope is bounded, not account-wide: `MinhHaDuong/{cadens,padme,fuzzy-corpus}`
      each return 404 under the new token and resolve under the classic one.
      `gh api user/repos --jq length` is *not* a usable check — a fine-grained
      PAT reads every **public** repository implicitly, so `CIRED/cired.digital`
      resolving proves nothing. Only a private repo discriminates
- [x] Write access confirmed reversibly: created `refs/heads/probe-token-scope`
      at `origin/main`'s SHA, deleted it, and confirmed zero matching refs
      remain. This is what the invariant below needs — a read-only token would
      have locked the agent out at the next push
- [x] Both application paths export it, which is the trap 0343 left: the
      `BASH_ENV` loader (`make` recipes) and `pipeline_loaders` →
      `pipeline_keystore` (`dvc repro`, bare `uv run python`). Each verified by
      the private-repo 404, not by reading the value. Default-deny holds:
      `AGENT_GH_TOKEN_CLIMATEFINANCE` itself is never exported
- [x] Live end-to-end: the repaired 0365 merge gate — which reads
      `AGENT_GH_TOKEN` to query reviews and labels — allowed PR #1239 under the
      new token
- [x] `make lint` and the credential suites pass (36 tests across
      `test_env_has_no_secret_literals`, `test_pipeline_keystore`,
      `test_check_reviews`). `make lint`'s 4 failures in
      `test_datapaper_archive_layout` are `origin/main`'s, reproducible on a
      branch with no commits, and belong to open tickets 0403/0384

## Invariants

- No credential value in any committed file, test output, or PR description.
- `.env` gains no literal; `tests/test_env_has_no_secret_literals.py` enforces it.
- Do not delete the classic PAT until the fine-grained one is confirmed working
  — a failed swap otherwise locks the agent out of the forge mid-session.

## Residual, deliberately left open

The classic PAT is still live in `~/.config/keys/github.env` under
`AGENT_GH_TOKEN`, now unreferenced by this project's `KEYS=` line. Revoking it
is the author's call, not this ticket's: other projects on this machine may
select `github:AGENT_GH_TOKEN`, and revoking would break them silently. The
account-wide blast radius this ticket set out to bound is bounded *for this
project* — the classic token no longer reaches it.

Two things worth knowing later:

- **Expiry is a scheduled outage.** Fine-grained PATs cannot be non-expiring
  (366 days maximum). Every agent forge operation — push, PR, the merge gate —
  stops on that date, with a 404 that looks like a permissions bug rather than a
  lapsed credential.
- **The merge gate now blocks the documented ticket-only fast path.** With the
  matcher repaired (0365), `.claude/hooks/check-reviews.sh` demands 2 review
  cycles, or 1 with the `review:trivial` label, on *any* `gh pr merge` — while
  `.claude/rules/git.md` says a tickets-only diff merges on `erg check` plus a
  collision scan, with no review requested. PR #1239 hit this. The label plus one
  procedural review clears it, which is consistent with 0365 option 3b, but the
  rule and the hook now disagree in writing and one of them should yield.

## Exit criteria

`AGENT_GH_TOKEN` is a fine-grained PAT whose access is limited to this
repository, the agent's forge operations still work under it, and the
data-management plan's claim that separation is by token scope is verifiable
against the live token.
